# Building ffmpeg-remux.wasm

`ffmpeg-remux.wasm` is [FFmpeg](https://ffmpeg.org)'s libavformat, libavcodec
and libavutil, which are licensed under the LGPL 2.1 or later, built as one
Emscripten side module. This page says how, so you can build your own from the
same source, or from a modified copy.

## What is published

- `ffmpeg-@FFMPEG_VERSION@.tar.xz`: the source that `ffmpeg-remux.wasm` is built
  from. Its SHA-256 is `@FFMPEG_SHA256@`.
- `FFmpeg-LGPL-2.1.txt`: the licence.
- `ffmpeg-remux.wasm`: the built module, and `SHA256SUMS` for these files.
- This page.

## Building it

You need the Emscripten SDK, version @EMSCRIPTEN_VERSION@.

1. Unpack the source and enter it.

2. Configure it. This flag set builds only what a copy-only remuxer needs, in
   position-independent code, under the LGPL:

   ```sh
   emconfigure ./configure @FFMPEG_CONFIGURE_FLAGS@
   ```

3. Build the three libraries:

   ```sh
   emmake make libavformat/libavformat.a libavcodec/libavcodec.a \
     libavutil/libavutil.a
   ```

4. Link them into one Emscripten side module. Save the list under "Functions the
   module exports" below as `exports.txt`: one name per line, as written (with
   the leading underscore that Emscripten expects).

   ```sh
   emcc libavformat/libavformat.a libavcodec/libavcodec.a \
     libavutil/libavutil.a \
     -sEXPORTED_FUNCTIONS=@exports.txt -o ffmpeg-remux.wasm @SIDE_LINK_FLAGS@
   ```

## Functions the module exports

A program that loads the module looks these up by name (without the underscore).
A replacement must export all of them, with the same signatures as in the FFmpeg
release above, and so must keep that release's ABI:

```
@EXPORTS@
```
